    "text": "To determine the amount of water wasted during one hour, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of drops in one hour.\n2. Determine the total volume of water wasted in one hour.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the number of drops in one hour.**\n\nThe faucet drips 10 times per minute. There are 60 minutes in one hour. Therefore, the number of drops in one hour is:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ drops/minute} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes/hour} = 600 \\text{ drops/hour} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total volume of water wasted in one hour.**\n\nEach drop contains 0.05 mL of water. Therefore, the total volume of water wasted in one hour is:\n\\[ 600 \\text{ drops/hour} \\times 0.05 \\text{ mL/drop} = 30 \\text{ mL} \\]\n\nSo, the amount of water wasted during one hour is \\(\\boxed{30}\\) mL.",
